  "body": "Refs #787 — Slice C only. This PR does **not** close #787: Slices D/E/F remain, and acceptance criteria 1–3 of the issue stay open until they land.\n\nQueue task 13060 (repo-health-code-pilot, lane code-j).\n\n## What\n\nAdditive rich/kitty browser encoder in `pkgs/id/web/src/world-keyboard.ts`:\n\n- New exported `richTerminalBytesForKey`, **unused by the UI** in this slice (inert, per design §6 row C). The legacy `terminalBytesForKey` and its tests are unchanged and remain the default path.\n- Escape is always `CSI 27 u` (never a bare ESC byte, which the profile decoder treats as Unknown); modified Enter/Tab/Backspace use their CSI-u functional codes (13/9/127), distinguishing Tab from Ctrl+i and Enter from Ctrl+m; Shift+Tab uses the canonical `CSI 9 ; 2 u`.\n- Arrows/Home/End keep legacy CSI letter bytes unmodified, `CSI 1 ; <mod> <letter>` modified; Delete/Insert/PageUp/PageDown and F1–F12 (new in the rich encoder) use CSI tilde forms.\n- Ctrl/Alt printable scalars are CSI-u with the **unshifted** codepoint and the full modifier parameter (Ctrl+Shift+A → `CSI 97 ; 6 u`, which Slice A's decoder normalizes to scalar `A` + Control); AltGr (Ctrl+Alt) printable input stays plain UTF-8 text, as in the legacy path.\n- Same exclusions as legacy: Meta/OS shortcuts, Dead/Process/Unidentified, multi-scalar committed text, and profile-Unknown keys (F13+, modifier-only keys) return null.\n\n## Tests\n\nExpectations mirror `doc/kitty-disambiguate-v1-fixtures.json` (the Slice A Roc `Key.parse_events` corpus); parity is decoded-event equality per design §4.4, and Slice D's oracle will decode this encoder's output with the actual Roc decoder.\n\n- `bunx vitest run src/world-keyboard.test.ts` — 20/20 pass (10 legacy unchanged + 10 new rich)\n- Full web suite: `bunx vitest run` — 667 passed, 9 skipped (30 files)\n- `bunx tsc --noEmit` — clean\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796741351&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7734&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7734&signature=fb3b1b03e06f911c30b46ef1b937393251283f401eff53ef7c3e5b59529b8828\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7734?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
